# Test: a SIGHUP reload whose config a registered validator rejects is refused,
#       and the daemon keeps running the config it already has.
#
# VALIDATES: spec-fixit-config-validators-bypassed-at-startup AC-2 -- Thomas
#            ruled on 2026-08-11 (Q-1) that the reload REFUSES. There is no
#            override and no force flag. The invalid value reaches no protocol
#            encoder, and the running daemon is not dropped for it.
# PREVENTS:  a reload that walks past the startup guard. A guard that only the
#            boot path enforces fails open on the next SIGHUP, which is the
#            shape spec-fixit-mgmt-listener-auth-guard AC-7 already had to close
#            for listeners.
#
# The replacement config is syntactically valid and its BGP half is
# byte-identical to the running one, so nothing about the peer session changes
# whether the reload is applied or refused. The only difference is a plugin
# block whose `use` leaf names a plugin this build does not register. That leaf
# is `type string { length "1..64" }` in
# internal/component/plugin/yang/ze-plugin-conf.yang, so nothing but the custom
# validator can refuse it: revert LoadConfig's ValidateCustomSections call and
# the stderr line below disappears.
#
# Thomas's ruling has two halves and each has its own fence:
#
#   the reload FAILS -- the stderr expectations below, which name the refusal
#   and the validator that produced it.
#
#   the daemon KEEPS RUNNING -- the SIGTERM after the SIGHUP, and exit code 0.
#   A daemon that died on the SIGHUP cannot take the SIGTERM (syscall.Kill
#   returns ESRCH and the peer fails the run) and cannot exit 0, because a
#   process killed by a signal or a panic reports neither. Reaching the end of
#   the checker proves NEITHER half on its own: the peer owes nothing past the
#   SIGHUP, so it exits clean whether the daemon lives or dies, and an EOF after
#   a sighup action is accepted by design (Checker.expectingClose,
#   internal/test/peer/checker.go). Shape taken from
#   test/reload/signal-quit.ci, which pairs action=sigterm with exit code 0.
#
# The refusal route carries no new machinery. LoadConfig returns an error,
# runReload (cmd/ze/hub/main_reload.go) turns it into "reload: parse config",
# clears the staged candidate, and returns before ReloadConfig, the provider
# refresh, or engine.Reload run. handleSIGHUPReload prints it and loops.

stdin=peer:terminator=EOF_PEER

# Connection 1: the peer's route plus EOR, proving the session is established
# before the reload is attempted.
expect=bgp:conn=1:seq=1:hex=FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF00300200000015400101004002004003040A0000014005040000006418C0A801
expect=bgp:conn=1:seq=1:hex=FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF00170200000000

# Swap in the config carrying the refused value, then SIGHUP. The SIGTERM that
# follows is the liveness fence: it is delivered to the same pid, in the same
# peer loop iteration, after the reload has been refused.
action=rewrite:conn=1:seq=2:source=invalid-validator.conf:dest=ze-bgp.conf
action=sighup:conn=1:seq=2
action=sigterm:conn=1:seq=2
EOF_PEER

stdin=ze-bgp:terminator=EOF_CONF
bgp {
	peer peer1 {
		connection {
			remote {
				ip 127.0.0.1
			}
			local {
				ip 127.0.0.1
				accept false
			}
		}
		session {
			asn {
				local 1
				remote 1
			}
			router-id 1.2.3.4
			family {
				ipv4/unicast { prefix { maximum 10000; } }
			}
			capability {
				graceful-restart disable
			}
		}
		behavior {
			group-updates disable
		}

		update {
			attribute {
				origin igp
				local-preference 100
				next-hop 10.0.0.1
			}
			nlri {
				ipv4/unicast add 192.168.1.0/24
			}
		}
	}
}
EOF_CONF

tmpfs=invalid-validator.conf:terminator=EOF_INVALID
plugin {
	internal p1 {
		use no-such-plugin-exists
	}
}

bgp {
	peer peer1 {
		connection {
			remote {
				ip 127.0.0.1
			}
			local {
				ip 127.0.0.1
				accept false
			}
		}
		session {
			asn {
				local 1
				remote 1
			}
			router-id 1.2.3.4
			family {
				ipv4/unicast { prefix { maximum 10000; } }
			}
			capability {
				graceful-restart disable
			}
		}
		behavior {
			group-updates disable
		}

		update {
			attribute {
				origin igp
				local-preference 100
				next-hop 10.0.0.1
			}
			nlri {
				ipv4/unicast add 192.168.1.0/24
			}
		}
	}
}
EOF_INVALID

cmd=background:seq=1:exec=ze-peer --port $PORT:stdin=peer
cmd=foreground:seq=2:exec=ze -:stdin=ze-bgp:timeout=25s

# The daemon refused the reload ...
expect=stderr:contains=reload: parse config: config validation failed
expect=stderr:contains=is not a registered internal plugin
# ... and was still there afterwards to take the SIGTERM and shut down cleanly.
# runYANGConfig returns 0 only from the signal loop's shutdown path
# (cmd/ze/hub/main.go), which a daemon that died on the SIGHUP never reaches.
expect=exit:code=0
